WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.640
To paraphrase noted scientist Dr. Heinz Doofenshmirtz,
“If I had a nickel for every time there

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.860
was a Safe-Class anomaly that manifests as
an absurdly long entity that’s stuck underground

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.499
and pops up at multiple points around the
world, I’d have two nickels.

00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:15.849
Which isn’t a lot, but it’s weird that
it happened twice.”

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:23.010
Incidentally, that happens to be the case
with SCP-1193, the Buried Giant, and SCP-2952,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.100
C.O.R.G.I.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:29.490
They’re a pair of mysterious creatures with
very thought-provoking similarities between

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.490
them.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:35.560
But while both are exceedingly long entities,
neither are particularly long stories, so

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.579
today, we’re giving you a rare SCP Explained
Anomaly Double Feature!

00:00:39.579 --> 00:00:43.640
Let’s begin with the first of our two very
long boys: SCP-1193.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:50.100
The exact nature of SCP-1193’s anomalous
qualities are challenging to define.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.320
It appears to have biological, spatial, and
even temporal elements.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:02.350
SCP-1193-01, the primary component of SCP-1193,
is a human arm that appears completely normal

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.810
in a genetic sense, but exhibits a freakish
length and bone structure.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.100
This absurdly long arm was first discovered
in a drainage pipe inside the basement of

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.650
a telephone switching station in Scottsdale,
Arizona, where it had somehow become trapped.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.960
How this anomaly was first discovered, or
by whom, is not recorded.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:25.520
Approximately ten centimeters below the drainage
gate of the pipe, the arm terminates in what

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.810
seems to be a human hand of indeterminate
gender that is unremarkable in both size and

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.810
structure.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:36.840
Upon initial examination, the Foundation believed
that the arm somehow threaded through 35 meters

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.010
of drainage pipe.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:42.840
But, the use of an endoscopic camera within
the pipe revealed that the reality is much

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.369
more severe.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:49.100
The arm extends to at least 71 kilometers
beneath the earth which is around double the

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.340
overall length of Scottsdale, Arizona, itself
- With elbows regularly spaced across every

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.509
four kilometers of arm.

00:01:56.509 --> 00:02:01.090
Elbows below a depth of 26 kilometers are
slightly retroflexed to accommodate a nine-degree

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.619
southward bend in the drainage borehole.

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:08.259
Interestingly, the arm was also somehow able
to pass through the Mohorovičić discontinuity

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:13.120
, which is the lower limit of the earth’s
crust and the volcanic-hot upper mantle.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.319
The arm could actually be longer than we’re
currently aware, but the Foundation doesn’t

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:22.880
have any technology hardy enough to follow
the arm all the way down into the earth.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:28.150
Conversations that Foundation staff have had
with what is believed to be SCP-1193-01 via

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:34.340
the use of SCP-1193-02, indicate that the
entity may have no thermoreception.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:39.120
It has described itself as being stuck in
environments that, contextually, should have

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.810
either extremely high or extremely low temperatures.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:47.239
This does not seem to register with SCP-1193-
01.

00:02:47.239 --> 00:02:51.800
This may serve as an explanation as to why
it is experiencing no discomfort, despite

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:57.120
the borehole temperatures having been measured
in excess of 674 degrees Centigrade.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.040
But what exactly is SCP-1193-02?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:10.970
SCP-1193-02 is a GPO 746 rotary telephone,
with a topaz yellow plastic exterior, manufactured

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:12.720
in 1971.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:16.510
Because of the physical dimensions of the
phone, it’s too large to have been delivered

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:22.700
from below via the borehole, so we know that
SCP-1193-01 didn’t put it there.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:27.620
The working theory of Foundation researchers
assigned to the 1193 case is that the phone

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:32.830
was installed here specifically to facilitate
communications with the trapped SCP-1193-01.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:38.870
It is attached to a conventional twisted-pair
line which enters the drainage pipe containing

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:47.880
SCP-1193-01 and descends parallel to SCP-1193-01
until endoscopy is no longer practicable.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.330
Who or what installed the phone?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.330
How?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.190
And to what end, beyond just chatting with
the entity?

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:58.820
The Foundation doesn't presently know and
the investigation is ongoing.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:05.060
One clue to the purpose of SCP-1193-02 is
the fact that its rotary dial has been permanently

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.680
glued in place, rendering it unusable for
any kind of outgoing calls.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.520
Instead, the phone only receives calls, and
the only calls it seems to receive are from

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.380
a being that seems to be SCP-1193-01.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:25.259
Every weekday, between 8:32 AM and 10:34 PM,
Mountain Standard Time, the phone will ring

00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:26.960
up to five times.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.949
When answered by a member of Foundation personnel,
an unidentified voice believed to be that

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:38.180
of SCP-1193-01 will willingly engage in conversation
with the person on the other end of the line.

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:43.719
The Foundation has used this opportunity to
question SCP-1193-01 about its own nature,

00:04:43.719 --> 00:04:48.069
but it’s impossible to really know how reliable
the entity’s answers are.

00:04:48.069 --> 00:04:53.020
The voice on the line always refers to itself
as a human being, and often mistakes the Foundation

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.960
personnel for authority figures such as doctors,
firemen, or police.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.080
As a result of this, the voice has been forthcoming
with information , and the interviews have

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:03.400
been relatively straightforward.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.639
There have been notable similarities between
the information that the voice voluntarily

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:14.499
gives about itself, and the known facts about
the condition of SCP-1193-01, lending credibility

00:05:14.499 --> 00:05:17.440
to the idea that they are one and the same.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.979
The Foundation fastidiously records conversations
with the voice, and has created a list of

00:05:21.979 --> 00:05:26.020
anomalous details the entity has surrendered
during the phone calls.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:31.240
These include having human features, but an
anomalous body plan, so the voice seems to

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:36.029
have all the right pieces for a human being,
but in a bizarre configuration.

00:05:36.029 --> 00:05:39.469
This may explain the extremely long, many-jointed
arm.

00:05:39.469 --> 00:05:44.849
Whatever species or subspecies this entity
is, it may not be alone, as the voice often

00:05:44.849 --> 00:05:49.659
refers to a “cousin” or some kind of other
relative who’s on the way to pick it up.

00:05:49.659 --> 00:05:54.659
The voice also often talks about its feelings
of discomfort or boredom at its state of being

00:05:54.659 --> 00:05:55.659
confined.

00:05:55.659 --> 00:06:01.039
It also makes reference to strange seismic
activity along the Little Chino Fault Complex,

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:05.849
an upper branch in the Elsinore Fault Zone
of Southern California, over 300 miles away

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:07.249
from Arizona.

00:06:07.249 --> 00:06:11.569
This may be because the source of the voice
is so far underground, it’s still able to

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:13.639
feel the tremors resonating upwards.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:18.309
But one of the most frequent trends of all
in these conversations is the voice venting

00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:24.229
frustration that its arm, or some other body
part, is stuck in an inconvenient place.

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:29.340
This list of places has been exhaustive, but
includes handcuffs, a jelly jar, a pipe, a

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:32.139
cast, or in one instance, a gopher hole.

00:06:32.139 --> 00:06:36.389
Naturally, this has been seen as a cause for
concern among Foundation staff.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:41.919
If SCP-1193 does have spatially anomalous
components, is it possible that someone could

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:47.110
find a seventy kilometer arm sticking out
of a gopher hole or a jelly jar some time

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.110
soon?

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.280
Only time will tell.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.539
The Foundation currently regards any information
about the physical form of the entity beyond

00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:57.399
the exposed section of arm reached via endoscopy
as provisional.

00:06:57.399 --> 00:07:01.619
In other words, they really have no idea what
they’re dealing with here, and are unlikely

00:07:01.619 --> 00:07:04.199
to find out for sure any time soon.

00:07:04.199 --> 00:07:09.990
Two phone conversations with the voice via
SCP-1193- 02 have been transcribed in the

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.909
addendum to 1193’s main file.

00:07:12.909 --> 00:07:17.639
Both are conversations between the voice and
Dr. Hassan Iqbal, Director of Research at

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:20.300
the local SCP Containment Site.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:26.149
In the first of the two conversations, recorded
on March 24th, 2008, Dr. Iqbal asked who was

00:07:26.149 --> 00:07:29.430
calling, and the voice identified itself as
“David.”

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:34.990
The voice, or “David”, appeared to be
in its usual state of frustration and distress.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.559
Incorrectly believing that Dr. Iqbal was a
medical doctor at the hospital he was currently

00:07:38.559 --> 00:07:43.080
trapped inside, David implored him to remove
the cast from his “bottom arm.”

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:48.979
When Dr. Iqbal questioned David on what exactly
a “Bottom arm” is, he responded with confusion.

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:54.830
When Dr. Iqbal told him that he was a research
scientist, not a medical doctor, David became

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:59.270
frustrated, implied that Dr. Iqbal was incompetent,
and hung up.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:04.270
The next recorded call between Dr. Iqbal and
the voice occurred exactly a year later.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:08.300
In this call, the voice incorrectly believed
that Dr. Iqbal was a fireman.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.389
The voice complained about having reached
into his oven to pull out some cakes, becoming

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:14.170
stuck in the process.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.029
He pleaded for help, saying that the oven
was a tight fit.

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:21.770
When Dr. Iqbal showed concerns about the potentially
high temperatures within the oven, the voice

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.479
didn’t seem to know what he meant.

00:08:23.479 --> 00:08:27.709
In the end, the voice became frustrated, and
resolved to instead call its cousin.

00:08:27.709 --> 00:08:29.970
It apologized, and hung up.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.839
Most calls appear to follow this general structure.

00:08:32.839 --> 00:08:36.829
Because of the static and incredibly subdued
nature of the anomaly, the Foundation has

00:08:36.829 --> 00:08:41.760
deemed that SCP-1193 poses no meaningful risk
of containment breach.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:45.330
As a result, it has been given the rare “Safe”
classification.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:51.100
In order to keep it properly contained, the
drainage borehole containing SCP-1193-01 is

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:57.490
capped with a tungsten steel grate, containing
a locking 2.5 centimeter endoscopy aperture,

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:01.400
meaning a small hole through which to feed
the endoscopic camera.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:06.079
Every 48 hours, the drainage borehole is inspected
with an endoscope for any further developments

00:09:06.079 --> 00:09:08.730
concerning the anomalous arm.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:14.009
Seismographic monitoring devices are posted
at 2, 7, and 11 kilometer depths alongside

00:09:14.009 --> 00:09:17.730
the SCP-1193-01 borehole.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:22.170
Seismic readings consistent with subterranean
movement are reported immediately to Site

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:23.510
Director Iqbal.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:28.500
In the event of what is referred to as a “Subterranean
Containment Breach”, researchers and guards

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.420
working around 1193 are ordered to perform
Protocol 473a.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.839
This involves severing SCP-1193-01 below the
fifth elbow and backfilling remaining portions

00:09:38.839 --> 00:09:43.160
of the borehole with pressurized concrete
to seal the hole forever.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:49.220
The SCP-1193-02 phone is monitored at all
times by a trained Foundation interrogator

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:56.759
and standard procedure dictates that SCP-1193-02
is to be answered on or before the third ring.

00:09:56.759 --> 00:10:00.350
During these calls, the interrogator will
attempt to elicit valuable information about

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:06.209
SCP-1193 from the voice and all valuable intel
will then be recorded and logged.

00:10:06.209 --> 00:10:12.019
The Buried Giant is one of the more perplexing
Safe-Class anomalies handled by the SCP Foundation.

00:10:12.019 --> 00:10:14.890
So much about its true nature is unknown to
this day.

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:19.370
But a concern that both we and the Foundation
share is not knowing where the entity’s

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:21.430
other limbs are currently residing.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:25.370
For all we know, they could be sticking out
of an oven, a gopher hole, or even a jelly

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:28.180
jar somewhere near you…weird right?

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:35.709
Well, if you think that is strange, let us
now introduce you to SCP-2952, or C.O.R.G.I.

00:10:35.709 --> 00:10:39.769
Trust us, if you’re not familiar with this
one already, you are not ready for the strange

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:42.149
turns this is about to take.

00:10:42.149 --> 00:10:43.660
In the simplest terms, C.O.R.G.I.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:48.500
is a cheerful Welsh pembroke Corgi with an
adorable face and a thick, shiny coat.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.829
He’s also over 30,000 kilometers in length,
with his head and front legs sticking out

00:10:52.829 --> 00:10:56.889
of the ground in Portland, Oregon, and his
hind quarters being all the way over in a

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:59.730
rural area of Japan's Kariwa District.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:04.680
His body weaves all across the globe, with
sections of it surfacing all over the Americas,

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.129
Europe, and much of Asia.

00:11:07.129 --> 00:11:13.230
Studies to find African or Australian sections
of SCP-2952 are still ongoing.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:17.199
Despite his massive length, there seems to
be no delay in reaction times, either.

00:11:17.199 --> 00:11:21.650
You pat his head in the USA, and his tail
will immediately start wagging over in Japan.

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:23.440
He’s honestly just precious.

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:28.730
He also doesn’t appear to need food or water,
and thanks to the somewhat sadistic experiments

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:33.560
of one Researcher Mills, we know that he can
quickly regenerate from all damage done to

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.560
him, too.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:39.100
Okay, now you’re familiar with this very
good albeit very long lad, it’s time for

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:41.259
things to get really, really strange.

00:11:41.259 --> 00:11:47.160
You see, on the different exposed sections
of SCP-2952’s body, there are tiny openings

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:51.100
designated SCP-2952-1.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.269
Stay with us here.

00:11:52.269 --> 00:11:57.680
There are 324 of these openings all over the
world, some in major cities, others in suburban

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.190
areas, some in the tiniest and most rural
of hamlets.

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:05.589
At this point, you probably have the very
reasonable question: Why are there over three

00:12:05.589 --> 00:12:07.569
hundred openings in this dog?

00:12:07.569 --> 00:12:11.360
Well, we’re going to answer that, but we
can’t promise it won’t just give you more

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.639
confusing questions.

00:12:12.639 --> 00:12:19.519
When the openings appear, humanoid beings
designated SCP-2952-2 will begin to exit the

00:12:19.519 --> 00:12:20.519
corgi.

00:12:20.519 --> 00:12:24.279
For the sake of clarity, we’ll refer to
these little creatures as the Welsh Fair Folk

00:12:24.279 --> 00:12:28.339
or the Fae, though there are many different
sub-groups of Fae.

00:12:28.339 --> 00:12:33.910
And we really do mean “Little” in this
case - On average, they’re a puny 3 centimeters

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:37.870
tall, and they’re also invisible to the
naked eye, with indirect methods like photographs

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.689
or videos being the only way to view them.

00:12:40.689 --> 00:12:45.519
Though they do leave evidence of their presence
beyond their direct physical appearances,

00:12:45.519 --> 00:12:47.230
like shadows or footprints.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:48.230
C.O.R.G.I.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:51.509
acts as a kind of transport system for these
little people.

00:12:51.509 --> 00:12:56.920
Openings on the dextrous side of SCP-2952
take passengers west, while those on the sinistrous

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.490
side take passengers east.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:02.690
Passengers can be seen entering and exiting
at regular intervals.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:06.410
The Foundation has even been able to track
a group of passengers getting on the C.O.R.G.I.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.170
transit system, and getting off at a later
stop.

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:14.010
From this, the Foundation has been able to
estimate that the speed of the system is 120

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:18.589
kilometers per hour, excluding stops to let
passengers on and off along the way.

00:13:18.589 --> 00:13:22.899
Which, for the record, is a pretty leisurely
pace by train standards.

00:13:22.899 --> 00:13:27.660
Naturally, the SCP Foundation weren’t exactly
thrilled to learn about an anomalous transit

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:31.459
system that worked to spread further anomalies
all over the world.

00:13:31.459 --> 00:13:34.760
In fact, that’s kind of a nightmare scenario
for them.

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:39.420
So they martialled their global forces, located
each of the openings along the torso of the

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.379
C.O.R.G.I. system, and blocked them up.

00:13:41.379 --> 00:13:45.350
At this point, the SCP Foundation were ready
to give themselves a pat on the back, close

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.699
up shop for the night, and go out for after-work
drinks.

00:13:48.699 --> 00:13:52.000
However, there was one thing that they’d
all forgotten.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:56.329
Hell hath no fury like a society of Welsh
Fae who’ve just had their daily commute

00:13:56.329 --> 00:13:57.329
ruined.

00:13:57.329 --> 00:14:01.470
The Council of Tylwyth Teg, their ruling body,
doesn’t take kindly to having their public

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.639
services messed with.

00:14:02.639 --> 00:14:07.329
And the manner of their retaliation was less
like a group of disgruntled anomalous civil

00:14:07.329 --> 00:14:10.439
servants, and more like a kind of Fae mafia.

00:14:10.439 --> 00:14:14.439
They would make the Foundation rue the day
they messed with C.O.R.G.I, with a series

00:14:14.439 --> 00:14:18.660
of retaliatory strikes that Groups of Interest
like the Chaos Insurgency and the Children

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.189
of the Scarlet King could only dream of.

00:14:21.189 --> 00:14:26.020
It began with the kidnapping of Project Director
Stevens, who’d authorized the containment

00:14:26.020 --> 00:14:27.020
project.

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:31.079
He vanished from his apartment and was replaced
with an adult European mole - Which seems

00:14:31.079 --> 00:14:35.970
to be the Fae equivalent of leaving a horse’s
head in the bed as “an offer you can’t

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:36.970
refuse.”

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:37.970
to send a message.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.220
But it didn’t stop there.

00:14:39.220 --> 00:14:44.209
Over the next three weeks, seventeen different
members of personnel - specifically, construction

00:14:44.209 --> 00:14:48.009
workers - who’d worked on the project woke
up to find that the walls of their houses

00:14:48.009 --> 00:14:52.250
had been entirely replaced by poison ivy and
death-cap mushrooms.

00:14:52.250 --> 00:14:57.439
And after two months, Researcher Mills - the
weird dog-torturer we told you about earlier

00:14:57.439 --> 00:15:02.459
- woke up with highly poisonous nightshade
berries in his mouth and hawthorn stakes driven

00:15:02.459 --> 00:15:05.829
through his hands and feet, crucifixion style.

00:15:05.829 --> 00:15:10.019
All perpetrated by some very upset three-inch
transport workers.

00:15:10.019 --> 00:15:13.710
At this point, the Foundation put together
who was behind these attacks, and decided

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:17.970
to try to make amends with the Fae whom they’d
understandably upset with their treatment

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.040
of C.O.R.G.I.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:24.879
A plan was drafted to have all the SCP-2952-1
entrances unburied.

00:15:24.879 --> 00:15:29.329
After this undertaking was completed, the
Fae retribution came to an end, and most of

00:15:29.329 --> 00:15:31.370
the damage was undone.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:33.629
Director Stevens was returned unharmed.

00:15:33.629 --> 00:15:36.040
The construction workers got their walls back.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.040
And…

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:41.290
Well, Researcher Mills didn’t get better,
but I think we can all agree that animal cruelty

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.999
isn’t really a crime that we should be forgiving
lightly.

00:15:44.999 --> 00:15:49.689
After all this chaos had transpired and the
SCP Foundation had fully made amends, Director

00:15:49.689 --> 00:15:54.299
Stevens had a note left on his desk by a starling,
which then flew off before it could be caught

00:15:54.299 --> 00:15:59.029
- By the way, can we just take a second to
appreciate that the SCP Foundation has contained

00:15:59.029 --> 00:16:04.769
literal demi-gods and interdimensional horrors
but Director Stevens was outfoxed by a bird.

00:16:04.769 --> 00:16:07.709
Wonderful, those Fae truly are built different.

00:16:07.709 --> 00:16:11.009
Anyway, the note on his desk, translated from
Welsh, read:

00:16:11.009 --> 00:16:15.680
“Thank you for your prompt response to commuter
complaints and wonderful customer service.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:19.510
As such, we have granted all members of your
organization complimentary transportation

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.329
on our C.O.R.G.I. system.

00:16:21.329 --> 00:16:25.800
Please send a sparrow to the Council of the
Sidhe office nearest you if you have further

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:26.800
questions.

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.199
G. Foxglove, Director of Transportation

00:16:29.199 --> 00:16:31.279
The Council of the Tylwyth Teg.”

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:35.689
And with tremendous relief that the slate
had finally been cleared, the Foundation decided

00:16:35.689 --> 00:16:40.040
that they would accept the kind offer extended
to them by the Council, and send one of their

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.240
field agents to take a look inside the C.O.R.G.I.
system.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:48.360
The Field Agent in question was Agent Elizabeth
Davies, chosen for her pleasing social skill

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.490
and proficiency in Welsh.

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:54.699
With the intention to take a ride in mind,
and connected to audio and video feeds linked

00:16:54.699 --> 00:16:58.410
back to central command, Agent Davies touched
the side of C.O.R.G.I.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:03.200
This caused her to shrink down to a height
of 3.2 centimeters, much like all the other

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:04.200
commuters.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:09.520
She stepped into the SCP-2952 entrance, and
found that on the inside, it looked not unlike

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:14.199
a regular train, though some carriages seemed
to be in disrepair and everything was written

00:17:14.199 --> 00:17:15.199
in Welsh.

00:17:15.199 --> 00:17:18.260
Oh, and everything was made with wood and
plant matter, too.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.959
The chassis appeared to be constructed from
birch, and all the seat cushions were made

00:17:21.959 --> 00:17:22.959
of flower petals.

00:17:22.959 --> 00:17:25.550
It was all very whimsical, honestly.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.799
Agent Davies struck up conversations with
some of the other commuters.

00:17:28.799 --> 00:17:31.120
One complained about delays caused by the
fact that C.O.R.G.I.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:35.380
was suffering from kidney stones - a problem
that the Foundation is eager to help the poor

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.710
animal get over to keep the transit system
running smoothly.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:42.520
She also chatted with a sweet elderly lady
on the train, who was getting people to sign

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:45.420
a petition to allow mice back onto the C.O.R.G.I.

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:46.450
transit system.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:50.840
When Agent Davies departed the system, she
patted the dog and told him he was a good

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.809
boy before returning to normal size.

00:17:53.809 --> 00:17:59.020
Since January 5th, 2017, the C.O.R.G.I. system
and its passengers became invisible to everyone

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:02.590
who wasn’t officially under SCP Foundation
employ.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:06.640
This has allowed for its reclassification
as a Safe-Class anomaly.

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:07.980
So there you have it, folks.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:11.950
At least one of our two Very Long Boys got
everything sorted out.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:15.940
We love occasionally doing a happy ending
here at SCP Explained.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:20.520
Remember to stay tuned for our next episode,
about the time that SCP-106 managed to get

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:21.970
onto a school bus!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:22.970
What?

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:25.110
We did say occasionally.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:30.940
Now go check out “Why Everyone Wants to
Eat this Corpse - SCP-1176” and “SCP-2935

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:36.320
O, Death and More Epic SCP Stories You Can't
Miss” for more bizarre anomalies that will

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.720
blow your mind!

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:37.820
So long, folks!

